        <p>Song titles in gold link to a full story on this site.</p>
        <p>Year is the year-end Hot 100 the song appears on, and Year-End Rank is its place on that list.</p>
        <p>The #1 Hit column and every date in the last column come from the weekly Billboard Hot 100 number ones, not from year-end rank.</p>
        <p>Prefer a hands-off listen? <a href="/radio/?play=1978-1-shadow-dancing">Open the same songs on Listen Now</a> and let the jukebox run.</p>

        <h2 id="answer">The Short Answer: What Makes a 70s Dance Song</h2>
        <p>A 70s dance song is a Billboard Hot 100 hit from 1970 to 1979 built around a groove that people moved to.</p>
        <p>The list below is tilted toward the disco floor, but it starts with Motown and funk.</p>
        <p>Here is what the list shows at a glance:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>{{DISCO_N}} of the {{N}} songs carry the disco tag in this site's song data.</li>
          <li>{{DANCE_TITLES}} titles name dancing outright, from "Dancing Machine" to "He's the Greatest Dancer."</li>
          <li>The longest run at number one is eight weeks, held by the Bee Gees' "Night Fever."</li>
          <li>{{N1}} songs reached number one, and {{NOT_N1}} stayed on the year-end lists only.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>These 70s Dance Songs Skip the Party Singalongs</h3>
        <p>No song here repeats on the companion <a href="/blog/songs/70s-party-songs/">70s party songs</a> list.</p>
        <p>That page leans on singalong hits like "Joy to the World" and "Y.M.C.A."</p>
        <p>This one keeps the tracks where the beat does the work.</p>

        <h2 id="method">How These 70s Dance Songs Were Chosen</h2>
        <p>The starting pool came from this site's own song data, which tags every year-end Hot 100 song for 1970 to 1979 with a vibe.</p>
        <p>{{POOL}} songs are tagged dance and have a YouTube video on record.</p>
        <p>From that pool, {{N}} made the list on three tests:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The song is not already on the 70s party songs list.</li>
          <li>Its chart facts can be checked against the weekly or year-end Billboard data on this site.</li>
          <li>Its chart line is computed from that data, never typed from memory.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>That is why the story column holds dates and neighbors, not trivia.</p>

        <h3>Where the Year-End Rank on These 70s Dance Songs Comes From</h3>
        <p>The Year-End Rank column is a position on that year's Billboard year-end list.</p>
        <p>It is not the song's weekly peak.</p>
        <p>"Da Ya Think I'm Sexy?" sits at 4 for 1979, yet it spent four weeks at number one.</p>
        <p>Not sure which of the {{N}} fits your night? The <a href="/pages/mood-song-matcher">Mood Song Matcher</a> works from this site's own mood tags.</p>

        <h2 id="title-words">Songs That Tell You What to Do</h2>
        <p>Plenty of 70s dance songs hand you the instruction in the title.</p>
        <p>Counting the {{N}} titles by the words that name a move or a scene shows how often it happened.</p>

        <div class="data-table-wrap">
          <table class="data-table">
            <caption>Dance words in the titles of the {{N}} 70s dance songs on this list</caption>
