        <h3>Dancing Is the Favorite Word</h3>
        <p>{{DANCE_TITLES}} of the {{N}} titles contain "dance," "dancing," "dancer" or "dancin'."</p>
        <p>"You Should Be Dancing" and "Shadow Dancing" both reached number one.</p>
        <p>"Dance, Dance, Dance (Yowsah, Yowsah, Yowsah)" did not, and sits at number 20 on the 1978 year-end list.</p>

        <h3>Boogie, Shake and the Disco Label</h3>
        <p>"Jungle Boogie," "Boogie Fever" and "Boogie Nights" carry the other favorite word.</p>
        <p>"(Shake, Shake, Shake) Shake Your Booty" and "Shake Your Body (Down to the Ground)" ask for the same thing a different way.</p>
        <p>Two titles use the word disco itself, "Disco Duck" and "Disco Inferno."</p>

        <h2 id="eras">Four Stretches of the Dance Floor</h2>
        <p>Grouping the {{N}} songs by the year-end Hot 100 they appear on shows where the floor filled up.</p>

        <div class="data-table-wrap">
          <table class="data-table">
            <caption>The {{N}} 70s dance songs by year-end Hot 100 period, with how many reached number one</caption>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Period</th><th>Songs on this list</th><th>Reached #1</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
{{ERA_ROWS}}
            </tbody>
          </table>
